{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/451852-mummy-the-einherjar-chronicle","id":451852,"title":"Mummy: The Einherjar Chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-21T12:00:55-07:00","id":451852,"title":"Mummy: The Einherjar Chronicle","content":"<span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Became inspired for a crossover Chronicle idea that I think would work best with a Mummy skeleton to hang things on. Also <i>Valkyrie Profile</i> is like one of my favorite games ever.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">DISCLAIMER: This gleefully throws out many of the core themes of Mummy and embraces a high-pulp, mythic tone. If you're not interested in that, that's fine; I know that this isn't your average Mummy chronicle. Or WoD Chronicle in general.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><u>The Einherjar Chronicle</u></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Arem-Abfu (or Usekh-Nemtet, they both work, plus free choice of Decree) is your Judge, but you've been given a specific, straightforward Purpose: During the fifth turn of the Sothic Wheel, there shall be a great battle, and an extra-dimensional army shall issue forth from their profane home to devour our world. You must gather an army of warriors to combat them. During your travels, find warriors of great strength, cunning, wisdom, honor, and purity. No stone shall remain unturned. These warriors may be damned corpses, half-spirit monstrosities, or fallen agents of an inscrutable arcane machine god.<br /> <br /> Basically, instead of hunting relics (or rather, in addition to) you'd be hunting allies from all over the planet and between the first and fifth sothic turns (because 3473 sounds like an awesome time period for mummies: Moon bases! Robots!). PCs would be the Mummy (possibly multiple mummies so you can tackle different locations during the same time period) and the cultists, plus the &quot;guest star&quot; supernatural warrior for that story. Spend a few sessions figuring out how to recruit the guest star, handle their problems, and then...I dunno, do some sort of ritual that shoots them into the future or something. They swear to serve in Arem-Abfu (or Usekh-Nemtet's) future army, is the point.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Criticisms (beyond the obvious ones that I brought up in the Disclaimer)?</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":1923,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","user":"BigDamnHero","date":". 03-21-2015, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T12:15:45-07:00","id":451881,"title":"","content":"Uhh, that sounds super awesome?<br /> <br /> Plus, you inherently have awesome hooks if you're trying to convince someone to travel x thousand years in the future. You have to finish ALL their unfinished business, promise to protect their families, their favorite dog, whatever/etc.<br /> <br /> Sounds like a good chance to also play with the themes of each supernatural.<br /> <br /> Oooh and you could have it be more free form! You can recruit generic fighters, but the SuperWar also needs specific roles filled. A dream warrior, for example. Then you can have several options to choose from. Do you recruit the changeling or the ... uhh other dream capable super?<br /> <br /> Build your dream team! Then play those characters in the final confrontation! (if you want)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}